==English==

===Etymology===
From a specialized meaning of {{m|en|cold}}, referring to lack of empathy.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-in cold blood.ogg|a=AU}}

===Prepositional phrase===
{{head|en|prepositional phrase}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} In a [[ruthless]] and [[unfeeling]] [[manner]], [[particularly]] as [[applied]] to [[first-degree murder]] [[commit]]ted without [[provocation]] and with [[malice aforethought]].
#: {{ux|en|It was not a suicide! He was murdered '''in cold blood'''.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/general/1841244/suspect-in-lop-buri-gold-robbery-murders-arrested|title=Suspect in Lop Buri gold robbery-murders arrested|date=2020-01-22|accessdate=2020-01-22|location=Bangkok|publisher=Bangkok Post Public Company Limited|work=Bangkok Post|text=Police have arrested a suspect in the murder-robbery of a gold shop in Lop Buri two weeks ago, in which a young child and two adults were killed '''in cold blood'''.}}

